# Bank 5 (runs at 0x8000). Directives: L label, C line comment, B block
# header, D data range, F row width.
#
# THIS BANK HOLDS NO CODE. It holds two things:
#
#   - the six-byte RECORDS with which routine 0x4371 in bank 0 loads the
#     scenery: a flag saying which third of the screen, the colour source,
#     the index of the character where it starts, the pattern source. A zero
#     flag ends the list.
#   - graphics compressed in the 0x49B9 format (tools/rle.py), just like the
#     whole of bank 4.
#
# The sources in the records point into this bank AND into bank 4, because
# both are mapped at the same time (the 4/5/6 split at p00:4234 and its
# copies). Walking the records gives 198 distinct sources, and all of them
# fall within 0x6000-0x9FFF.

B 0x8000 GRAPHICS AND LOADING RECORDS (bank 5)

D 0x8000 0x86BB graphics_chain_8000  Chain of 20 compressed blocks that fit with no slack, from 0x8000 to 0x86BA. They are requested by the records of this same bank.
F 0x8000 16
D 0x86BB 0x8FCB graphics_per_stage  Seven compressed blocks in a row (0x86BB, 0x8A8C, 0x8C1E, 0x8D27, 0x8E4B, 0x8ECA, 0x8F3E). They are handed out by table 0x42B3 of bank 0: two blocks per stage, each with the index of the character where it starts.
F 0x86BB 16
D 0x8FCB 0x91D1 graphics_1D00  Two blocks: 0x8FCB, which 0x4287 dumps into VRAM 0x1D00, and 0x9038, which table 0x42B3 asks for for stage 5.
F 0x8FCB 16
D 0x91D1 0x92E3 object_shapes  Four bytes per shape: the object's two top characters and its two bottom ones. 0x48CB reads them indexing with (IX+0x0C)*4, and writes them to the name table 0x1E apart.
F 0x91D1 4
D 0x92E3 0x92FB record_lists_A  Twelve words, one per stage: where that stage's list of 0x4371 records starts. Read by 0x4306 with 0x47AE (DE = word at HL+2*A).
F 0x92E3 w2
D 0x92FB 0x9313 record_lists_B  Twelve words, one per stage. Read by 0x4316.
F 0x92FB w2
D 0x9313 0x932D record_lists_C  Thirteen words, one per stage. Read by 0x4320.
F 0x9313 w2
D 0x932D 0x938E common_records  Sixteen six-byte records and the 0x00 that ends them. Loaded by 0x42FC in every stage.
F 0x932D 6
D 0x938E 0x939B extra_records_1  Two six-byte records and their 0x00. Loaded by 0x432B, and only when 0xF0F4 is not zero.
F 0x938E 6
D 0x939B 0x93A8 extra_records_2  Two six-byte records and their 0x00. Loaded by 0x4337, and only from stage 9 onwards.
F 0x939B 6
D 0x93A8 0x98A3 records_per_stage  The record lists that the three tables above point to, one after another: 0x93A8, 0x9403, 0x9434, 0x9477, 0x94D8, 0x9527, 0x9546, 0x95BF, 0x961A, 0x963F, 0x9664, 0x9689, 0x96AE, 0x96C7, 0x96EC, 0x96F9, 0x9712, 0x972F, 0x9733, 0x9750, 0x9779, 0x9782, 0x979F, 0x97B4, 0x97C9, 0x97FE, 0x9837, 0x9838, 0x9865 and 0x988E.
F 0x93A8 6
D 0x98A3 0x98B0 trigger_records  Two six-byte records and their 0x00, loaded by 0x4A86.
F 0x98A3 6
D 0x98B0 0x98B9 list_for_0x4348  Nine bytes that 0x4A92 passes to 0x4348 in IX. A different format from the 0x4371 records.
F 0x98B0 9
D 0x98B9 0x9963 extra_records_graphics  Five compressed blocks of 34 bytes (0x98B9, 0x98DB, 0x98FD, 0x991F, 0x9941): the patterns and colours requested by the records at 0x938E and 0x939B.
F 0x98B9 16
D 0x9963 0x9BE4 graphics_names_1800  Compressed block that 0x4296 dumps into VRAM 0x1800 (the name table) when 0xF0F4 is not zero.
F 0x9963 16
D 0x9BE4 0xA000 filler  0xFF filler up to the bank's 8192 bytes.
F 0x9BE4 16
